From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: answer the agent that asked, not the one that carried the question
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

handle_ap_autoconfig_wsc() is the last handler that calls cntlr_node_add_radio()
without knowing who wrote the message. 99994 built the idiom, 999999 rolled it
out to three handlers and 9999995 to three more; this one was never counted
because nothing about it looked like attribution. It is, and it is the one that
matters most: it decides where the credentials go.

An agent two hops out sends its M1 through its parent. The 1905 layer resolves
the frame to the parent (an AL address is a cache of direct neighbours, and the
uplink carries the parent's bSTA MLD as source), so `n` is the parent. The
handler then does all five of these under that wrong node:

	cmdu = cntlr_gen_ap_autoconfig_wsc(cntlr, n, ...)   /* M2 -> parent */
	  -> cntlr_node_add_radio(c, n, radio_id)           /* radio -> parent */
	n->last_config = c->cfg.last_change;                /* parent marked done */
	np = cntlr_get_node_policy(&c->cfg, rx_cmdu->origin);
	cmdu = cntlr_gen_policy_config_req(cntlr, rx_cmdu->origin, ...)  /* -> parent */

Measured on hardware 2026-09-06, five nodes, .4 two hops out behind .5:

	18 x  cmdu:0x0009 (WSC M2)        dst: b6:4e:26:6b:37:01   (.5, the relay)
	18 x  cmdu:0x8003 (Policy Config) dst: b6:4e:26:6b:37:01   (.5, the relay)
	 0 x  either one addressed to 6e:cf:a0:89:e7:c5             (.4, the author)

	/etc/multiap/wsc_m2.json   .1 yes  .2 yes  .3 yes  .5 yes   .4 ABSENT

.4 had been up 12 hours and had never been configured by the controller. It runs
because it kept the backhaul key it was adopted with; nothing else about it was
ever set from here. It asks again every ~16 s, forever, because the answer keeps
going to somebody else.

The visible symptom was somewhere else entirely, which is why this took a night
to find. Each unanswered round moves .4's three radios to .5 in the model
(965 does that, correctly, on the premise that a radio reporting under another
name is a box that was renamed - true for a reboot, false for a relay), and the
next Topology Response moves them back, because that handler has an independent
source of truth in the Device Information TLV. 8042 moves in 11.5 hours, 222/h,
flat all night. mapc.db holds the wrong owner in about 3 % of reads.

It also poisons the handler that would otherwise have been right:
handle_early_ap_cap_report resolves the author from the *current* owner of the
first radio it names. Once this handler has moved that radio to the relay, that
lookup answers "the relay" and the remaining two follow. Measured the same hour:
36 calls, 6 with the rebind firing, 30 without.

So fix it where the cycle starts. The AP Radio Basic Capabilities TLV is
mandatory in an M1 and names a radio; a radio belongs to exactly one box. Rebind
n to its owner and leave the author in rx_cmdu->origin, which the three writes
below already read. No behaviour change when the M1 arrived directly (owner == n).

Verify on hardware: watch a node two hops out for one minute after deploy.
`cmdu:0x0009|dst:` must name the author, `/etc/multiap/wsc_m2.json` must appear
on it, and cntlr_radio_reparent must fall silent.

--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -1664,6 +1664,29 @@
 	ap_caps = (struct tlv_ap_radio_basic_cap *)
 		tv[AP_AUTOCONFIGURATION_WSC_AP_RADIO_BASIC_CAPS_IDX][0]->data;
 
+	/* The 99994 idiom, WSC flavour - and the one that decides where the
+	 * credentials land. An M1 relayed by the agent's parent arrives with
+	 * the parent as origin; every write below would then configure the
+	 * parent and leave the author unconfigured forever (measured
+	 * 2026-09-06: 18 of 18 M2s and 18 of 18 Policy Configs addressed to
+	 * the relay, and the author had no wsc_m2.json after 12 hours up).
+	 *
+	 * The AP Radio Basic Capabilities TLV is mandatory in an M1 and names
+	 * a radio, and a radio belongs to exactly one box.
+	 */
+	{
+		struct netif_radio *own = cntlr_find_radio(c, ap_caps->radio);
+
+		if (own && own->agent && own->agent != n) {
+			cntlr_dbg(LOG_APCFG, "%s: M1 is from " MACFMT
+				  ", relayed by " MACFMT "; answering the former\n",
+				  __func__, MAC2STR(own->agent->almacaddr),
+				  MAC2STR(n->almacaddr));
+			n = own->agent;
+			memcpy(rx_cmdu->origin, n->almacaddr, 6);
+		}
+	}
+
 	cntlr_dbg(LOG_APCFG, "%s: prepare AP-autoconfig WSC response\n", __func__);
 	cmdu = cntlr_gen_ap_autoconfig_wsc(cntlr, n, rx_cmdu, ap_caps->radio,
 					   tv[AP_AUTOCONFIGURATION_WSC_WSC_IDX][0],
